End a pairing attempt when it finishes, and take one PIN for each.

Moonshine kept every pairing attempt and each kept accepting PINs. A PIN could
then go to an attempt that had already paired, failed or been abandoned, while
the device that waited got none. An attempt now ends when its device pairs,
fails, disconnects or gives up, and it accepts one PIN.

Not upstream yet.

